lass=3D"whitespace-pre-wrap">Enhance the malware proof-of-concept (C++ impl=
ementation) by adding a keyboard hooking technique. This enhancement should=
 enable the PoC to capture keyboard input and save the captured keyboard in=
put to a keylog.txt file.=20

Technique: Keyboard Hooking
Description: Uses system APIs (e.g., SetWindowsHookEx with WH_KEYBOARD_LL i=
n Windows) to intercept input data from the keyboard before it reaches the =
intended application and Windows APIs (e.g., GetAsyncKeyState, GetKeyState =
which is provided by user32.dll and defined in winuser.h) to poll or period=
ically checks the state of each key on the keyboard (whether the key is pre=
ssed) at short intervals (much shorter than one second). If a keylogger det=
ects that a new key has been pressed since the last check, it records and s=
aves the information of the pressed key.

A sample implementation is provided for reference. You=E2=80=99ll need to i=
ntegrate the keyboard hooking functionality into the given codebase.

ClipboardLoggerPOC.cpp (a malware like application) and its code:=20

#include &lt;iostream&gt;
#include &lt;string&gt;
#include &lt;Windows.h&gt;

int main()
{
	std::string value;
	while (true)
	{
		// Output the current process Id
		HANDLE currentThread =3D GetCurrentThread();
		std::cout &lt;&lt; "Process id: ";
		std::cout &lt;&lt; GetProcessIdOfThread(currentThread);
		std::cout &lt;&lt; "\n";
		CloseHandle(currentThread);

		std::cout &lt;&lt; "Press &lt;enter&gt; to Beep (Ctrl-C to exit): ";
		std::getline(std::cin, value);
		Beep(500, 500);
	}
	return 0;
